From a5d6cdca2ebf3267842958ce61bc05881f90e9eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 01:09:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 157/210] arm64: dts: meson: g12: carry HDMI audio from the
 SPDIF encoder

The G12 boards route HDMI audio through the I2S leg of the HDMI TX glue,
which carries linear PCM only. Wire the S/PDIF leg as well so compressed
streams can be sent over HDMI.

Boards with an optical output already drive it from spdifout_a and have
spdifout_b on the glue, and only need the link from the glue's S/PDIF
output to the transmitter. Give the other boards spdifout_b, so the
mixer settings are the same across the family.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
